492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (More recently, the focus has shifted to representation learning in a latent space, e.g. through contrastive losses \(van den Oord et al., 2018; He et al., 2020; Chen et al., 2020\), negative-free similarity \(Grill et al., 2020; Chen & He, 2021\), online clustering and self-distillation \(Caron et al., 2020; 2021; Li et al., 2021\). For all these methods, data augmentation is a key component. In particular, we regard the popular multi-crop strategy as a crude suggestion of objectness , as it implicitly encourages learning similar representations between the global view of an object and a cropped view of its  parts. Although recent extensions introduce patch-based contrastive learning \(Li et al., 2021; Wang et al., 2021\), the resulting features remain redundant. How to summarize dense features into sparse representations is an area of active research \(Hinton, 2021\).)
/E (More recently, the focus has shifted to representation learning in a latent space, e.g. through contrastive losses \(van den Oord et al., 2018; He et al., 2020; Chen et al., 2020\), negative-free similarity \(Grill et al., 2020; Chen & He, 2021\), online clustering and self-distillation \(Caron et al., 2020; 2021; Li et al., 2021\). For all these methods, data augmentation is a key component. In particular, we regard the popular multi-crop strategy as a crude suggestion of objectness , as it implicitly encourages learning similar representations between the global view of an object and a cropped view of its  parts. Although recent extensions introduce patch-based contrastive learning \(Li et al., 2021; Wang et al., 2021\), the resulting features remain redundant. How to summarize dense features into sparse representations is an area of active research \(Hinton, 2021\).)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
